      *> kb/Work PB1499 -- ISO 9.3.8.2.3 rule 5 a) (cite.py --check 9.3.8.2.3 "If the returning item in interface-2 is
      *> a universal object reference, the corresponding returning item in interface-1 is an object reference" ->
      *> OK 9.3.8.2.3 5) a)): where interface-2's RETURNING item is universal, interface-1's may be ANY object
      *> reference -- universal, class-typed, INTERFACE-typed or ACTIVE-CLASS.  Interface-1 is a class implementing
      *> interface-2's prototype (11.8.4 / 9.3.11) AND a method overriding the overridden one (11.7.3 SR9, cite.py
      *> --check 11.7.3 "the rules of conformance according to 9.3.8.2.3" -> OK 11.7.3 9)), so both paths are
      *> exercised for every kind: C1..C4 IMPLEMENT the IJ prototype GETIT, O1..O4 (and O5 under O3) OVERRIDE
      *> B's MAKE.  The result is invoked in every case, so the output is the returned object's own SHOW: K-SHOW for
      *> the KCV object every other leg builds, C4-SHOW / O4-SHOW where the ACTIVE-CLASS leg returns SELF.
      *> The INTERFACE-typed legs (C3, O3, O5) were a backend compile error before PB1499 (CS0266 in the covariant
      *> adapter, CS0508 on the override): the C# type of an interface-typed reference does not convert to the
      *> universal class type without a cast.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB1499RC.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       REPOSITORY.
           CLASS C1CV CLASS C2CV CLASS C3CV CLASS C4CV
           CLASS BCV
           CLASS O1CV CLASS O2CV CLASS O3CV CLASS O4CV CLASS O5CV
           INTERFACE IJCV.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 OC1 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE C1CV.
       01 OC2 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE C2CV.
       01 OC3 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE C3CV.
       01 OC4 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE C4CV.
       01 OO1 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE O1CV.
       01 OO2 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE O2CV.
       01 OO3 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE O3CV.
       01 OO4 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE O4CV.
       01 OO5 USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE O5CV.
       01 OB USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE BCV.
       01 IJ USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE IJCV.
       01 UR USAGE OBJECT REFERENCE.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           INVOKE C1CV "NEW" RETURNING OC1.
           SET IJ TO OC1.
           INVOKE IJ "GETIT" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           INVOKE C2CV "NEW" RETURNING OC2.
           SET IJ TO OC2.
           INVOKE IJ "GETIT" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           INVOKE C3CV "NEW" RETURNING OC3.
           SET IJ TO OC3.
           INVOKE IJ "GETIT" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           INVOKE C4CV "NEW" RETURNING OC4.
           SET IJ TO OC4.
           INVOKE IJ "GETIT" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           INVOKE O1CV "NEW" RETURNING OO1.
           SET OB TO OO1.
           INVOKE OB "MAKE" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           INVOKE O2CV "NEW" RETURNING OO2.
           SET OB TO OO2.
           INVOKE OB "MAKE" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           INVOKE O3CV "NEW" RETURNING OO3.
           SET OB TO OO3.
           INVOKE OB "MAKE" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           INVOKE O4CV "NEW" RETURNING OO4.
           SET OB TO OO4.
           INVOKE OB "MAKE" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           INVOKE O5CV "NEW" RETURNING OO5.
           SET OB TO OO5.
           INVOKE OB "MAKE" RETURNING UR.
           INVOKE UR "SHOW".
           STOP RUN.
       END PROGRAM PB1499RC.

       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
